00:32:33,481 --> 00:32:37,480
the mine's method for storing them is state-of-the-art.

467
00:32:37,481 --> 00:32:39,480
As everything moves into the digital world,

468
00:32:39,481 --> 00:32:41,480
we'll continue to still store the old films,

469
00:32:41,481 --> 00:32:45,980
films, but we also get involved in the digitization of the films with the studios.

470
00:32:45,981 --> 00:32:51,440
Everything's barcoded and then that barcode ties into a location number that

471
00:32:51,441 --> 00:32:55,100
we have on the shelving rack and then that's all put in our computer systems.

472
00:32:55,101 --> 00:33:00,680
That job falls to the facility's 58 person staff who spend 40 hours a week

473
00:33:00,681 --> 00:33:06,360
in a very ordinary looking office, only it's buried 600 feet beneath the earth.

474
00:33:06,361 --> 00:33:11,200
But for all the classic movies, and crate after crate of government documents,

475
00:33:11,740 --> 00:33:15,320
the storage facility takes up just a fraction of the Hutchinson Mine.

476
00:33:17,420 --> 00:33:21,420
We're going to take a left and head into the mine where we're mining salt.

477
00:33:22,180 --> 00:33:26,880
The rest is still devoted to harvesting America's most important mineral.

478
00:33:27,760 --> 00:33:30,140
There's several lifetimes of salt here.

479
00:33:30,840 --> 00:33:34,000
Myron Markock is the manager of the Hutchinson Salt Mine.

480
00:33:34,001 --> 00:33:40,020
The mine is two and a half miles north to south and a mile and a half east to west and is growing every day.

481
00:33:40,400 --> 00:33:43,780
I pretty much got this mine mapped out for the next 40 years.

482
00:33:44,440 --> 00:33:51,320
Working in almost total darkness, miners here will unearth nearly 5 million pounds of salt in a single day.

483
00:33:52,600 --> 00:33:56,820
But if the miners remove too much salt, the mine could collapse on itself.

484
00:33:56,821 --> 00:34:00,200
So as the salt they've harvested is hoisted to the surface,

485
00:34:01,300 --> 00:34:04,100
miners leave huge pillars of salt to hold up the ceiling.

486
00:34:06,700 --> 00:34:09,300
It's a job the crew here takes very seriously.

487
00:34:10,180 --> 00:34:13,260
After all, without them, some of our most beloved movies

488
00:34:13,261 --> 00:34:17,680
and our government's most guarded documents might be lost forever.

489
00:34:23,420 --> 00:34:26,340
The Hutchinson Mine isn't the only site in the Midwest

490
00:34:26,341 --> 00:34:29,300
that's found at dual use is a secret underground?

491
00:34:29,301 --> 00:34:33,180
Welcome to the Marengo Distribution and Warehouse Center.

492
00:34:33,181 --> 00:34:35,580
Unlike most distribution facilities,

493
00:34:35,581 --> 00:34:38,580
this one is 160 feet below the surface.

494
00:34:38,581 --> 00:34:40,580
Most people think that when you say

495
00:34:40,581 --> 00:34:42,500
we're going to take you underground,

496
00:34:42,501 --> 00:34:45,980
they think that you're going to go down, if you will,

497
00:34:45,981 --> 00:34:48,300
and you do not go down in this facility.

498
00:34:48,301 --> 00:34:51,100
This is all a level facility,

499
00:34:51,101 --> 00:34:53,580
from the parking lot all the way back.

500
00:34:53,581 --> 00:35:01,880
Each day, more than 40 semis rolling to access the many loading docks housed in this 4 million square foot former limestone quarry.

501
00:35:02,480 --> 00:35:07,640
My favorite thing about driving a truck in a cave is there aren't too many people doing it.

502
00:35:07,980 --> 00:35:10,360
Most people that drive are, you know, outside.

503
00:35:10,700 --> 00:35:16,220
And many of the drivers here are headed deep inside, where the mission is saving lives.

504
00:35:16,580 --> 00:35:22,060
Each one of these boxes that you see behind me, around, contains meals like these.

505
00:35:22,061 --> 00:35:29,400
This is Brian Venturi, manager of the Marengo Warehouse and Distribution Center, the man

506
00:35:29,401 --> 00:35:34,180
who keeps this subterranean storage area humming 24 hours a day.

507
00:35:34,181 --> 00:35:38,543
Like the Hutchinson salt mine, one of Brian's biggest clients is the U.S.

508
00:35:38,544 --> 00:35:39,244
government.

509
00:35:39,245 --> 00:35:43,600
But instead of housing valuable documents, the Marengo Warehouse works in conjunction

510
00:35:43,601 --> 00:35:44,510
with the U.S.

511
00:35:44,511 --> 00:35:50,460
military and with relief organizations like FEMA and the Red Cross to supply disaster

512
00:35:50,461 --> 00:35:54,100
victims with MREs, or meals ready to eat.

513
00:35:54,660 --> 00:36:00,140
Each one of these pallets behind us contains 48 cases, and as you can see, we have quite

514
00:36:00,141 --> 00:36:01,540
a few of these meals in inventory.

515
00:36:02,680 --> 00:36:07,720
The MREs held at the Marengo Warehouse's underground facility don't stay here long.

516
00:36:08,660 --> 00:36:13,140
Thanks to their fleet of forklifts and pallet loaders, the warehouse is capable of loading

517
00:36:13,141 --> 00:36:18,960
up more than 100 tractor trailers a day with MREs, which can lead to that rarest of sights,

518
00:36:18,961 --> 00:36:22,700
a traffic jam several hundred feet below ground.

519
00:36:23,560 --> 00:36:28,160
We take a lot of pride in being available 24-7 around the clock

520
00:36:28,161 --> 00:36:31,440
to be able to help the victims of whatever disaster might occur.

521
00:36:32,400 --> 00:36:35,060
For a company that provides disaster relief,

522
00:36:35,540 --> 00:36:39,180
it helps that its distribution center is also disaster-proof.

523
00:36:39,920 --> 00:36:45,060
That's due in large part to the warehouse's 167-foot-thick limestone ceiling.

524
00:36:45,061 --> 00:36:51,380
Since I've been here and we have been through three or four earthquakes within a 75-mile radius of here,

525
00:36:51,800 --> 00:36:55,300
and didn't even know that we had one, it's a very, very safe place to be.

526
00:36:59,420 --> 00:37:03,380
This next subsurface structure wasn't engineered to save lives.

527
00:37:04,140 --> 00:37:08,040
Instead, it housed a bumper crop of illegal activity.

528
00:37:08,041 --> 00:37:16,640
Montreal, Canada is home to two cities, one above ground and one below.

529
00:37:17,520 --> 00:37:21,040
With over 20 miles of tunnels spread across five square miles,

530
00:37:21,780 --> 00:37:28,620
the underground city, known as Rezo, contains apartments, shopping malls, and even a university.

531
00:37:29,620 --> 00:37:32,520
Secret Underground will return on Modern Marvels.

532
00:37:33,040 --> 00:37:37,240
We now return to Secret Underground on Modern Marvels.

533
00:37:38,040 --> 00:37:45,280
Some of the most sophisticated secret undergrounds in the world are buried beneath the most unlikely of structures.

534
00:37:46,400 --> 00:37:53,280
Case in point, this A-frame house in central Tennessee, an area known for its many limestone caves.

535
00:37:53,920 --> 00:37:59,700
It may look like an ordinary house from the outside, but underneath it lies a hidden labyrinth.

536
00:38:01,000 --> 00:38:06,180
Caves that for a decade concealed one of the most complex criminal enterprises in the country.

537
00:38:08,040 --> 00:38:15,420
It started in 1996, when a local resident began construction on a house right next to a large limestone cave.

538
00:38:16,240 --> 00:38:20,640
At first, everything seemed normal, until a few months later,

539
00:38:20,900 --> 00:38:25,180
when neighbors noticed some pretty bizarre activity in the cave next to the house.

540
00:38:26,540 --> 00:38:29,860
The sheriff's department had a complaint of a bulldozer in the cave,

541
00:38:30,020 --> 00:38:32,840
and once we met Mr. West, we knew there was something wrong.

542
00:38:33,540 --> 00:38:35,420
I had a suspicion he was up to no good.

543
00:38:35,421 --> 00:38:38,520
Sheriff's deputies kept a close eye on the property.

544
00:38:39,460 --> 00:38:43,880
Construction continued, and bulldozers periodically showed up in the nearby caves.

545
00:38:46,720 --> 00:38:52,900
Then, in 2005, the local utility company noticed a substantial amount of electricity

546
00:38:52,901 --> 00:38:55,540
being siphoned off the power grid near the home.

547
00:38:56,220 --> 00:38:59,380
The stolen electricity was enough to justify a search warrant.

548
00:38:59,381 --> 00:39:05,580
Here we are coming down the driveway into what would have been the original structure.

549
00:39:06,700 --> 00:39:08,520
This was once the garage right here.

550
00:39:08,660 --> 00:39:11,400
When you come to this corner of the garage, there was a closet.

551
00:39:11,660 --> 00:39:14,460
It would appear to just be an ordinary, normal closet.

552
00:39:14,580 --> 00:39:20,560
But in this particular closet was this hidden box, which had this secret control panel.

553
00:39:20,880 --> 00:39:23,860
When sheriff's officers flipped the switch on the control panel,

554
00:39:23,861 --> 00:39:27,640
a giant steel door

555
00:39:27,641 --> 00:39:30,020
powered by a massive hydraulic system

556
00:39:30,021 --> 00:39:31,920
slowly began to open.

557
00:39:33,020 --> 00:39:34,660
A big door with big hydraulics

558
00:39:34,661 --> 00:39:36,260
means there's something big on the other side.

559
00:39:37,380 --> 00:39:39,500
Behind the vault door was a ramp

560
00:39:39,501 --> 00:39:43,060
that led the officers 120 feet underground

561
00:39:43,061 --> 00:39:46,980
to another set of steel doors.

562
00:39:47,620 --> 00:39:49,720
Before we opened the double doors at the bottom,

563
00:39:49,860 --> 00:39:51,240
we could smell what was on the other side.

564
00:39:53,860 --> 00:40:00,860
Spanning the length of two football fields and spread out over several bunker-like rooms

565
00:40:00,861 --> 00:40:06,860
was the largest underground marijuana operation ever discovered in the United States.

566
00:40:06,861 --> 00:40:10,471
When we walked in, it was like you was walking into a laboratory.

567
00:40:10,472 --> 00:40:11,860
The place was immaculate.

568
00:40:11,861 --> 00:40:16,860
Not only was the cave immaculate, it was also a marvel of underground engineering.

569
00:40:16,861 --> 00:40:22,860
An elaborate hydroponic growing system kept the marijuana plants stable in the subterranean environment.

570
00:40:22,861 --> 00:40:28,200
and a heating and ventilation system kept the cave at a tropical 82 degrees.

571
00:40:29,280 --> 00:40:32,580
We're in the room where the actual groves took place.

572
00:40:32,860 --> 00:40:36,300
The plants were on a series of tables in various stages of growth.

573
00:40:36,700 --> 00:40:40,460
The pot cave also had a working septic system and living space,

574
00:40:41,000 --> 00:40:42,840
capable of housing up to eight people.

575
00:40:43,460 --> 00:40:46,260
The attention to detail in the construction of it was amazing.

576
00:40:46,900 --> 00:40:49,880
Equally as amazing was the series of escape tunnels,

577
00:40:49,881 --> 00:40:53,360
carved out of solid limestone that led to the surface.

578
00:40:54,500 --> 00:40:56,540
You had an escape hatch here,

579
00:40:57,760 --> 00:40:59,520
and when you go through the escape hatch,

580
00:40:59,600 --> 00:41:02,820
there was actually a room up here between here and the surface.

581
00:41:03,600 --> 00:41:06,160
The room contained food, water, supplies

582
00:41:06,161 --> 00:41:08,540
where a person could stay in that room for a period of time.

583
00:41:09,460 --> 00:41:13,700
And then from that room, there was a vertical tunnel leading straight up,

584
00:41:13,701 --> 00:41:18,180
which you could open that up, and the outside of the hatch was actually a fake rock.

585
00:41:19,880 --> 00:41:26,680
The pot cave was so sophisticated that authorities estimate it cost nearly $1 million to construct.

586
00:41:27,540 --> 00:41:34,140
After seizing it, local officials sold the subterranean compound at auction for nearly $300,000.

587
00:41:35,620 --> 00:41:39,260
The former pot cave turned out to be the perfect location

588
00:41:39,261 --> 00:41:47,620
for a Midwest cheesemaker who needed to expand underground.

589
00:41:49,880 --> 00:41:53,140
Welcome to Emmy Roth Case in Monroe, Wisconsin.

590
00:41:54,820 --> 00:41:57,180
100 feet below the main sales floor,

591
00:41:59,440 --> 00:42:01,940
cheesemakers are working in a climate-controlled cellar,

592
00:42:02,740 --> 00:42:05,420
producing 60,000 wheels of cheese a year.

593
00:42:06,280 --> 00:42:10,340
To do that, the cellar must be kept at a constant 55 degrees

594
00:42:10,341 --> 00:42:13,520
with 95% humidity year-round.

595
00:42:14,080 --> 00:42:18,220
The aging time for the Gruyere is a minimum of four months.

596
00:42:18,221 --> 00:42:26,820
That product ages all the way out until the flavor profile stops developing and can be 10 months, can be 12, 14, even 16 months old.

597
00:42:27,340 --> 00:42:33,000
These are difficult conditions to regulate, but they exist naturally in the pot cave in Tennessee.

598
00:42:33,680 --> 00:42:36,160
That's why Emmy Rock Case purchased the cave.

599
00:42:37,860 --> 00:42:42,700
In 2011, the pot cave is slated to reopen as a cheese seller.

600
00:42:42,701 --> 00:42:51,320
But instead of criminals growing acres of marijuana, a robot named Sam, designed specifically

601
00:42:51,321 --> 00:42:56,060
to work in an underground environment, will be tending wheels of cheese.

602
00:42:57,680 --> 00:42:58,660
This is Sam.

603
00:42:58,860 --> 00:43:01,020
Sam stands for semi-automatic smearing machine.

604
00:43:01,580 --> 00:43:03,540
This is one of the first ones like it in the U.S.

605
00:43:03,640 --> 00:43:08,360
Sam is like a giant pallet jack with a lot of technology thrown into it.

606
00:43:08,361 --> 00:43:11,800
Sam takes the product, brings the board out of the rack,

607
00:43:12,140 --> 00:43:14,460
brings the product down, pushes the cheese off,

608
00:43:14,980 --> 00:43:18,100
flips the cheese over, and then sets it on pedestals,

609
00:43:18,280 --> 00:43:20,320
and as the pedestals are turning, the cheese is turning.

610
00:43:20,940 --> 00:43:22,760
There's a side brush and a top brush,

611
00:43:22,900 --> 00:43:25,220
and it's smearing or washing the rind of the product.

612
00:43:26,120 --> 00:43:26,920
He's very efficient.

613
00:43:30,300 --> 00:43:31,940
Whether they're filled with food

614
00:43:31,941 --> 00:43:35,040
or buried under our borders,

615
00:43:36,300 --> 00:43:37,860
concealed under casinos,

616
00:43:38,360 --> 00:43:42,060
or carved out of mountains of salt,

617
00:43:43,560 --> 00:43:45,880
America owes much of its identity

618
00:43:45,881 --> 00:43:49,040
to the unseen network of high-tech tunnels

619
00:43:49,041 --> 00:43:53,380
and one-of-a-kind caverns that lie beneath our feet.

620
00:43:54,420 --> 00:43:56,860
They are our secret underground.

